page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Recovery & verification · FokoLab 80.1</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="styles/recovery.css"><style>body{font:16px/1.65 system-ui;max-width:1050px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 22px}h1{line-height:1.2}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}td,th{padding:10px;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #bcc}</style><body><a href="index.html">← FokoLab</a><h1>Original animation recovery</h1><p>FokoLab 80.1.0 integrates the actually served plant, leaf, cell, lipid, random-process and evolutionary applications. Original animation and numerical source files are hash-checked; they were not approximated from screenshots.</p><p>The existing analytical laboratories and simpler teaching modules remain available. Their models are not interchangeable. The source reports version 82.0-instrument; this GitHub integration follows the separate 80.0 release lineage.</p><h2>Preserved scientific source</h2><p>'''+str(len(checks))+''' engine, renderer, worker, state-description and scientific style/data files are copied byte for byte. The retrieval manifest also records failed candidate URLs; these include guessed export names and are not all required runtime dependencies.</p><nav class="recovery-paths"><a href="plants/index.html">Plant growth</a><a href="leaf/index.html">Leaf physiology</a><a href="tcells/index.html">Cell lineages</a><a href="lipids/index.html">Lipid reactions</a><a href="random.html">Random processes</a><a href="continuum/advanced.html">Evolution journey</a><a href="continuum/approaches.html">Evolution & search</a><a href="continuum/index.html">Haploid evolution</a></nav><h2>Evidence</h2><p><a href="recovery-manifest.json">Source and transformation manifest</a> · <a href="recovery-tests.json">Executed test results</a></p><p>Passing software tests does not validate biological parameters, prove a bistability interpretation, or establish experimental agreement. Browser runs are headless Chromium checks, not physical-device or unfamiliar-user studies. Old release evidence applies only to its stated release.</p><h2 id="exports">Export and access limits</h2><p>Native JSON, CSV, image and figure-export controls are retained. The original host refused three advertised ZIP archives with HTTP 403: its full-site ZIP, plant Python ZIP and leaf Python ZIP. Their contents have not been recovered or replaced with invented native-Python implementations. The existing additional teaching modules retain their own separately labelled Python exports.</p><p>Private planning PDFs and font binaries are excluded from newly recovered distributions. The existing public Scientific Mastery companion remains accessible. Historical weather calls require their external data service; an offline or failed response is not silently replaced by synthetic weather.</p><h2>Saved experiments</h2><p>Existing record schemas are preserved. A different website origin cannot read the old site's browser storage. Export a record on that site and import it in <a href="research/index.html">the recovered saved-experiment workspace</a> to move personal runs.</p><p><a href="experiments.html">Complete experiment catalogue</a> · <a href="saved-experiments.html">Saved runs</a> · <a href="book.html">Public book companion</a></p></body></html>'''
